      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_City%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "After an explosion flooded and burned the town, residents moved and renamed it Spring City in honor of the original settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_City%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Spring City began as a stop along the Cincinnati Southern Railroad in the 1870s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_City%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original wooden depot burned in 1892 and was replaced by a larger one, which later became the current depot completed in 1909.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_City%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1942 the Tennessee Valley Authority finished Watts Bar Dam and its reservoir southeast of town, giving Spring City an economic boost.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
